1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,740
You open TikTok, a video plays instantly, you

2
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:07,740
swipe, and another appears. Now imagine millions of

3
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:09,630
people doing this at the same time. How

4
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:11,780
would you design a system that makes every

5
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:14,790
swipe feel effortless? We can break a TikTok-like

6
00:00:14,790 --> 00:00:18,100
platform into four main parts, video upload, video

7
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:22,380
processing, video delivery, and the recommendation engine. Let's

8
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:25,170
follow one video through the system. First, a

9
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:28,750
creator taps upload. The app sends a request

10
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:31,120
through an API gateway, which checks authentication and

11
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,910
directs the request to an upload service. The

12
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:36,730
video file goes into object storage, while details

13
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:39,380
like the creator, caption, and upload status go

14
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:42,070
into a metadata database. But the raw file

15
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:44,600
isn't ready for everyone to watch. The upload

16
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,120
service places a job on a message queue.

17
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:50,040
Background workers pick it up. Compress the video

18
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:53,600
into several resolutions, generate thumbnails, and run safety

19
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,990
checks. Using this work into a queue means

20
00:00:55,990 --> 00:00:58,310
a sudden spike in uploads won't overwhelm the

21
00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:01,490
app. Now someone opens their 4U feed. The

22
00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:03,990
app requests a batch of recommended video IDs

23
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:06,910
from a feed service. The service retrieves video

24
00:01:06,910 --> 00:01:09,100
details, but it doesn't send the actual video

25
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:12,610
bytes from the main database. Instead, playback comes

26
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:15,670
through a content delivery network, or CDN. A

27
00:01:15,670 --> 00:01:18,060
CDN keeps copies of popular video data on

28
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:21,630
servers closer to viewers, that reduces delay, and

29
00:01:21,630 --> 00:01:23,510
the app can pre-load the next video while

30
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:25,890
you're watching the current one. This is why

31
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:29,630
Swiping can feel almost instantaneous, but which video

32
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:32,540
appears next? That's where recommendations come in. A

33
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:35,950
recommendation system can start with candidate videos, then

34
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:38,560
rank them using signals like watch time, likes,

35
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:42,760
skips, shares, and information about the videos themselves.

36
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:45,250
TikTok has publicly described using these kinds of

37
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:48,920
signals, though its exact internal design isn't public.

38
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:51,510
Every swipe also creates new data, an event

39
00:01:51,510 --> 00:01:55,730
pipeline collects interactions, updates analytics and user interest

40
00:01:55,730 --> 00:01:59,150
features, and makes fresh signals available for future

41
00:01:59,150 --> 00:02:01,760
recommendations. Likes and comments can be handled by

42
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:04,520
separate services, so they don't slow down playback.

43
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:08,590
Finally, how does this scale? Load balances spread

44
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:12,560
requests across servers, caches avoid repeated database reads.

45
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:15,740
Workers can scale independently when uploads spike, while

46
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:18,260
CDN servers absorb much of the video traffic,

47
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:21,280
so the key insight isn't one giant supercomputer.

48
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:24,750
It's a collection of specialized services, connected by

49
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:28,030
APIs and queues, designed so uploading, recommending, and

50
00:02:28,030 --> 00:02:30,080
watching videos can all happen at once.

